# Customising & validating records

## Compact constructor — validate & normalise

Record name, **no parameter list**, runs before the field assignments:

```java
public record Temperature(double celsius) {
    public Temperature {
        if (celsius < -273.15)
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("below absolute zero");
    }
}
```

Reassign a component to **normalise** — `value = value.strip();` flows into the final field.

## Methods & static factories

```java
public record Point(int x, int y) {
    public double distanceTo(Point o) { return Math.hypot(x-o.x, y-o.y); }
    public static Point origin() { return new Point(0, 0); }
}
```

Instance methods, static factories, static constants — all fine.

## Guard mutable components

```java
public Team { members = List.copyOf(members); }   // defensive copy → truly immutable
```

**Line to hold:** keep it a *value* — no mutable fields, no identity. Needs a lifecycle? Make it a class.
